A||||16||Tom88gt||carparts.com sucks||||8||
Z||000000||Tom88gt||05-11-2000||05:18 PM||||Guys, I hate to start a flame but this really bites.<P>4/27/00 I ordered a set of ignition wires for my girlfriend's Mazda.<P>5/4/00 CarParts.com sends me an email "not available and will send a substitue".  <P>5/11/00 I call customer service and it hasn't shipped yet.  It's "not on back order", just hasn't gone out yet.  Thats BS.<P>I'll just get them at NAPA at 3 times the price (they're in stock).  She can't go without a car for a lousy $40 bucks.<P>If you need a part to get back on the road, skip these guys.  If it's your second car, it might be worth the wait but it better be big savings.<P>Buyer beware.||||reg||8
Z||000001||Robert||05-11-2000||11:38 PM||||Hey Tom;<BR>Sorry to hear about your troubles with CarParts.com.  I’ve used them many times without much trouble.  My last order with them was for a thermostat and a fan switch.  They shipped them within a few days, but separately, because of backorders.  I would still use them in the future, heck I even have their Fiero banner on my web page.  <A HREF="http://www.canterburytrails.com/page3.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.canterburytrails.com/page3.html</A> <BR>I guess there is some truth in the old adage “you are only as good as you last order”<P>Keep the faith<P>Robert<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||2M4 Dale||05-12-2000||02:04 AM||||Try wrenchead.com. I've had good luck with them and they are cheap and they send nice stickers for your toolbox...lol||||reg||14
Z||000003||Tom88gt||05-12-2000||08:38 AM||||I've looked at wrenchhead.com Ok prices but their web site is not as user friendly as carparts.com but that don't make up for slow, poor service.  I may still use them for  accessories if their price is too good to pass up but never for an important part again.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||05-12-2000||09:42 AM||||Give them another try with something you can live without.  Maybe this was an isolated incident.  I'd heard rumors that the Fiero Store was slow.  I ordered a poly bushing kit for my dogbone.  Got it in a couple of days.  Packaged nicely, etc.  I'll order from them in the future if I can't find something cheaper (kinda expensive, but they have things no one else does.).  I'd make sure I called (no email-not personal enough) their customer service department and <B>calmly</B> explained the problem.  Maybe they can do something about it and maybe they can't, but at least the problem will be documented.  Just my .04 cents (gotta allow for inflation).||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tom88gt||05-12-2000||12:44 PM||||Well I called customer service.  That was after my email hadn't been answered for 7 days <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  That's when they finally told me it still hadn't shipped.  14 days total now.  WTF?  I've placed other orders from them, a car cover which I don't mind waiting for, still hasn't arrived.<P>As for the Fiero Store, I've never ordered from them, yet.  But I'll cut ANY business which specialized in the Fiero a lot of slack before they loose my business  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||mshill||05-12-2000||01:27 PM||||I've had good luck with wrenchhead.com and not such good luck with JC Whitney.<P>What I like about wrenchead is the no tax and free shipping.  Their prices are just slightly better than the local autozone, but when I am buying a lot of stuff or expensive stuff, the local sales tax is a killer.<P>JCW on the otherhand, stiffs you on the shipping even if it is UPS ground (5-7 days).||||reg||1
Z||000007||deceler8||05-14-2000||03:26 PM||||I can't recall ever using Carparts.com where I wasn't frustrated with them at some point. <P>But they always redeem themselves...offer a substitution or a break on next order or something...<P>IMO they don't have their systems working very well yet but they do try to work with you if there's a problem.||||reg||1
Z||000008||DJRice||05-15-2000||09:13 AM||||I just put step bars on my Jeep and I bought them from CarParts.com.  The only problem I had was the standard email they send out with the tracking number did not have the correct tracking number on it.  Other than that, the experience was Good.  <P>Where else could I get step bars delivered to my door for $150. (15% off + free shipping)<P>Sign up for Carparts Enewsletter and youll get a coupon every month.  <P>BTW, Carparts has a toolbox sticker as well.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Old Lar||05-15-2000||12:06 PM||||I ordered some stuff from the Fiero Store last weekend from their web site. It was deliverd by Tuesday.  Can't complain.<P>||||reg||10
Z||000010||theogre||05-15-2000||11:09 PM||||Only ordered once from them. (there is a review of them and Wrenchead in this forum)<P>It was Accell 140017 coils for DIS. Had no problem at all with them businesswise. <P>Their online catalog is not entirely correct or completely wrong for DIS motors at times. <P>The Online help people were excelent, some of the best I've ever seen. They spent about half an hour finding the Accell coils for me. (Thier internal database was under construction at the time I think.) They even called me after 9PM eastern to finish the ordering and credit card transaction.<P>The packaging for shipment wasn't the greatest. May have been that one warehouse. (Carparts and wrenchead have several warehouses around the country.)<P>ON the other hand Wrenchead carries Borg Warner parts. I've found tho that Pep Boys prices are always within a couple dollars so I just get them there.<P>I forget which, wrenchead or carparts also has ACdelco. Usually less than dealler prices. (no-one but dealers seem to have anything but ACdelco oil filters around here.)<P>Tom88gt, sometimes ____ happens. I fix computers. You wouldn't believe the crap I got thru every day to get parts.<P>Toshiba, sometimes it's there next day, other stuff takes 2 weeks, and they can never tell you which it will be. Order three items get 2 and be held up on 1. This is IF the customer filled in the warrantee registration. If they don't register the computer then it's a guaranteed week delay for that paperwork.<P>Apple, Order exchange parts on one form. order "consumables" on another but enter them on the first form if you want to get your warrantee money. If you return a part god help you if you do it wrong. (They finally are reducing some of the return paper at least. Only took 16 years.)<P>Compaq, ships nearly everything overnight. Rare when they backorder. Unless it's a consumer line(presario) PC. Then you could wait awhile.<P>Dell, and some others, You can fix some products but others have to be sent to the "factory" for repair.<P>Packard Bell/NEC is pulling out much of it's north american operation. You can't get the same answer twice out of them when you call. Yes, you can fix it, then No, you can't fix it you have to send it to us.<P>E machine, Everyting is standard in the box but the $2 power supply and the box. The Fan in the power supply is worth maybe $0.50. It will fail. Good luck getting a new one.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 05-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Uaana||05-16-2000||01:00 AM||||Well I hope you guys are happy about making me paranoid about ordering from carparts.com, guess I'll stick with Summitracing who might not list all the stuff for our cars in their catalog but if you call them they can usuall find it in about 5min and give a good price which is usually cheaper than carparts since they dont pay comissions to banner owners and such. they also give you a bunch of goodie stickers and "stuff". My expierence with the fiero store is about the same as everyone else little more in price but Great service.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Greg Piet||05-16-2000||03:31 AM||||Well I am currently a little miffed at checker.   I looked up on their website that they had holley side scoops in their database and actually gave a price.  Normally when they cant get something they have the price as NA.<P>Since they had a price I went to a checker and  asked them if they could get one of these.  They said "Oh SURE!"  so I ordered one, and then they called me back a week after and said "Uhhh we cant get that part".  I wasnt too disappointed since I know the scoops aren't being made, but if that was a part i really needed I would have been hosed!<P><BR>oh well I was hoping I could get one from checker for only 16 bucks, then sell it on ebay for $3000.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||Tom88gt||05-17-2000||05:01 PM||||Still no car cover.  It was supposed to ship 5/9.  I've sent 2 emails asking if it actually shipped yet.  No response.  I guess accessories take as long as critical parts, too long.  Oh, the wires showed up anyway.  Even after I spoke with customer service, canceling the order because it still hadn't shipped.  So they shipped after it was canceled.  <P>I haven't passed final judgment yet.  I won't buy a critical part but I'm still giving accessories a chance.||||reg||9
Z||000014||terryk||05-18-2000||11:50 AM||||If you are buying a custom fit quality car cover, expect to wait 8-12 weeks. The factories are all backed up. I waited 10 weeks for the Noah for my GTP.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Tom88gt||05-23-2000||01:22 PM||||Called again yesterday.  Still no change.  the customer service rep said I would get an email update in a day or 2.  It's not a custom cover.  Just a Budgelite brand universal cover for my Jeep/small sport utes which I would think they would have in stock.  My local parts store can order the same one but it costs......a whopping 12 bucks more.  I'd still like to see if carparts.com can come through on this one.||||reg||9
Z||000016||Tom88gt||06-01-2000||04:58 PM||||I finally got my car cover today.  Almost a 4 week wait but I'm happy now.  I think I'll try them again later but ONLY for accessories.||||reg||7
